SUMMARY:Cranksgiving
DESCRIPTION:Lancaster Bicycle Club (LBC) Meetup\n## Overview\n\nPresented 
 byLititz Bikeworks and Stauffers of Kissel Hill\nThis is not an LBC event\
 n\nNo cost [Register](https://www.bikereg.com/cranksgiving-lititz) here.\n
 \nThat's what Lititz Bikeworks' Cranksgiving is all about. It costs absolu
 tely nothing to register and you get so much in return. Like the ride itse
 lf. You'll love the scenic spin through the most beautiful Amish farmland 
 in Lancaster County\, including covered bridges and the fall foliage along
  the WERT rail trail. All we ask is that you purchase non-perishables at e
 ach grocery stop along the route.\nBrought to you by **[Stauffers of Kisse
 l Hill grocery stores.](https://www.skh.com/)**\nThis year we have two rou
 tes available for you to ride\; A 30-mile rolling route stopping at three 
 grocery stores\, and for those who want a hilly challenge there is a 40 mi
 le Covered Bridge option that stops at one grocery store. There will be a 
 donation area at each grocery store where you can place your purchases (no
  worries about carrying them with you on your ride. The goal here is to fe
 ed as many families as possible\, not to weigh you down!).\nThis year\, Cr
 anksgiving is continuing our reach and will benefit two non-profit organiz
 ations that connect people in need with resources\; ***Manheim Central Foo
 d Pantry*** and ***Ephrata Area Social Services***. We're so impressed wit
 h the heart and soul of these local organizations\, each does so much for 
 local families. The ride this year is brought to you by Stauffers of Kisse
 l Hill. For over 80 years\, they have been offering customers high quality
  food\, home and garden products\, and services in central Pennsylvania un
 der the brand that has become known as Stauffers of Kissel Hill.\nThere wi
 ll be a mass start at 9:00am\, and Collusion Tapworks will be serving up h
 ot sandwiches\, sides and cold beers at Lititz Bikeworks from 11-1. We are
  giving away a gravel bike at the end of the day\, so enter the raffle and
  stay for the drawing!\nWe can't wait to ride with you on November 7th!\n-
 The team at Lititz Bikeworks and our gracious sponsor\, ***Stauffers of Ki
 ssel Hill***
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/lancaster-bicycle-club/events/3172199
 44/
