SUMMARY:York Heritage Trail 32 miles flat RSVP Required
DESCRIPTION:Lancaster Bicycle Club (LBC) Meetup\n**Join your friends on a 
 ride from the Wilmington Club and Lancaster club.**\n**Let’s do the Heri
 tage trail in reverse for a change. At 1pm let’s begin riding the trail 
 from New Freedom Train Station\, North toward York to the Brillhart Statio
 n and back.**\n**Optional:**\n**Returning to New Freedom**\n**1) Stopping 
 at Four Spring’s Winery**\n**2) At Railroad\, almost at the end stopping
  at Ale Craft Brewery**\n**This is a casual trail ride. Please do not go o
 n this ride unless you will stay with the group.** **We will ride as a gro
 up with no one left behind. Like always every rider must wear a helmet and
  have a tube that can be used to fix a flat.**\n**For the Lancaster Member
 s: To eliminate passing around a pen and paper waiver\, we encourage LBC C
 lub membership and Meetup RSVP below to join this ride. RSVP also allows u
 s to contact you after the ride if needed. If you do not RSVP you are not 
 covered by the club excess accident insurance policy\; only club members w
 ho RSVP are covered. Being on Meetup does not mean you are a club member. 
 Join here- [https://www.lancasterbikeclub.net/content.aspx?page_id=60&club
 _id=257148](https://www.lancasterbikeclub.net/content.aspx?page_id=60&club
 _id=257148)**\n**Richard Conner\, leader717-572-8480**
