SUMMARY:Impromptu Ride -  BI Linden Coffee (23F) RSVP Required
DESCRIPTION:Lancaster Bicycle Club (LBC) Meetup\nRide leader: Joanie N.\nS
 weep: (volunteer to sweep!)\nAnticipated Average Pace: \\~11 mph\nRoute: [
 BI Linden Coffee (23F)](https://routes.lancasterbikeclub.net/cue/bi-linden
 -coffee-23f/)\nYou can cut the route in half by returning on Old Philadelp
 hia Pike from Linden Coffee 3/4 mile to Bird-in-Hand Restaurant on your ow
 n.\n**Be Safe\, Have Fun\, and Ride Together**\n\n[Linden Coffee](https://
 drinklindencoffee.com/) will be open\, but Bird-in-Hand Restaurant will no
 t.\n\nThe ride leader will ride at the advertised average speed. This is i
 ntended to be a group ride with a no-drop rule as the main goal. The ride 
 leader will do his/her best to keep the group together with occasional reg
 roupings and/or splitting into multiple groups to align to pace capabiliti
 es.\n\nPlease do not join this ride if you are not willing to ride with th
 e group.\nHelmets are mandatory. No earbuds. Please bring water and a basi
 c repair kit (spare tube\, tire levers\, pump/CO2 inflator).\nTo eliminate
  passing around a pen and paper waiver\, we require LBC Club membership an
 d Meetup RSVP below to join this ride. Being on Meetup does not mean you a
 re a club member. Join here [Member Signup](https://www.lancasterbikeclub.
 net/content.aspx?page_id=60&club_id=257148)\nYour RSVP is your agreement t
 o abide by the club's Code of Conduct: [Code of Conduct](https://www.lanca
 sterbikeclub.net/content.aspx?page_id=22&club_id=257148&module_id=323984)\
 nGuidance if an incident occurs: [Incident Actions](https://lancasterbikec
 lub.net/content.aspx?page_id=22&club_id=257148&module_id=326137)
